---

<ApplicationLayout
  hideBottomCTA={true}
  title="Alfa Laval BTPX 205 Disc Centrifuge | Stainless Steel, Self-Cleaning"
  heroTitle="Alfa Laval BTPX 205 Disc Centrifuge"
  disableTitleSuffix={true}
  description="Alfa Laval BTPX 205 disc centrifuge specs, applications, and operation for liquid-solid separation and chemical processing."
  heroImage="/images/alfa-laval-btpx-205-disc-centrifuge/Alfa-Laval-BTPX-205-Hero-2000.webp"
  heroImageAlt="Alfa Laval BTPX 205 Disc Centrifuge"
  category="products"
  categoryLabel="Products"
  categoryHref="/alfa-laval-centrifuges/"
  canonicalUrl="https://dolphincentrifuge.com/alfa-laval-btpx-205-disc-centrifuge/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  toc={toc}
  relatedProducts={relatedProducts}
  relatedApplications={relatedApplications}
>

  <!-- Overview -->
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>

  <figure class="not-prose mb-6">
    <img
      src="/images/alfa-laval-btpx-205-disc-centrifuge/Alfa-Laval-BTPX-205-SGD34-CDP-1-600.webp"
      alt="Alfa Laval BTPX-205-SGD34-CDP"
      loading="lazy"
      width="600"
      height="640"
      class="img-cap-600"
    />
    <figcaption><strong>Alfa Laval BTPX-205-SGD34-CDP</strong></figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>The Alfa Laval BTPX-205 is a self-cleaning centrifuge of the disc-stack type. Its design allows it to separate the liquid from liquid and solids (purifier) or liquid from solids (clarifier).</p>

  <p>The BTPX-205 features a 'partial solids' ejection feature that allows the centrifuge to purge only the solids. This feature reduces fluid losses associated with sludge ejection.</p>

  <p>The sludge ejection cycle can be timer-triggered or based on the volume processed.</p>

  <p>The centrifuge separates suspended solids such as fine chemicals as a clarifier. When set up as a purifier, it separates solids and intermixed and immiscible liquid phases.</p>

  <p>For the BTPX 205, the solids content in the process fluid can be up to 10% by volume.</p>

  <figure class="not-prose mb-6">
    <img
      src="/images/alfa-laval-btpx-205-disc-centrifuge/Alfa-Laval-BTPX-205-SGD-34-CDP-600.webp"
      alt="Alfa Laval BTPX 205 SGD-34-CDP"
      loading="lazy"
      width="600"
      height="781"
      class="img-cap-600"
    />
    <figcaption><strong>Alfa Laval BTPX 205 SGD-34-CDP</strong></figcaption>
  </figure>

  <!-- Specifications -->
  <h2 id="specifications">Specifications</h2>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8 not-prose">
    <SpecTable
      model="alfa-laval-btpx-205"
      variant="striped-card"
      rows={[
        { label: 'Model Type', field: 'modelType' },
        { label: 'Maximum Capacity', capacity: 0 },
        { label: 'Sludge Space', field: 'sludgeVolumeGal' },
        { label: 'Bowl RPM', field: 'bowlSpeedRpm' },
        { label: 'Motor HP:', field: 'motorHp' },
        { label: 'Voltages:', field: 'voltages' },
      ]}
    />
  </div>

  <!-- Applications -->
  <h2 id="applications">Applications</h2>

  <p>The BTPX-205 is applicable for removing suspended solids with a particle size of 0.5 t0 500 µm. The liquid centrate has a lower density than the solids.</p>

  <p>For the BTPX 205, the solids content is usually in the range of 0,1 to 10% by volume. The total solids content can be from 0.1% to 10% by volume.</p>

  <p>The following are some of the popular applications of the Alfa Laval BTPX-205:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Chemical</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Precipitate Recovery</li>
        <li>Catalyst Separation</li>
        <li>Sub-micron Particle Separation</li>
        <li>Pigments, Dyes and Toners</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p><br>The maximum process capacity of the machine is 5 Gallon/Minute.</p>

  <!-- Operation -->
  <h2 id="operation">Operation</h2>

  <p>The process fluid enters the rotating bowl of the BTPX 205 centrifuge. The bowl exerts a high g-force on the process fluid.<br><br>The centrifugal force causes rapid sedimentation of the solids. These separated solids are auto-ejected from the centrifuge.</p>

  <p>The liquid phase moves towards the centers and exits the bowl through a separate outlet.</p>

  <p>A detailed explanation of the operation of the BTPX-205 centrifuge follows.</p>

  <figure class="not-prose mb-6">
    <img
      src="/images/alfa-laval-btpx-205-disc-centrifuge/BTPX-205-Bowl-Cross-Section-400.webp"
      alt="BTPX 205 Bowl Cross Section"
      loading="lazy"
      width="400"
      height="400"
      class="img-cap-400"
    />
    <figcaption><strong>BTPX 205 Bowl Cross Section</strong></figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>The process fluid enters the rotating bowl of the centrifuge through a stationary inlet pipe (1). The distributor (2) accelerates the fluid before it enters the disc stack (3).</p>

  <p>The separation of the solids from the liquid happens in the inter-disc space.</p>

  <p>The clear liquid moves towards the center of the bowl. A paring disc (4) pumps out the clear centrate.</p>

  <p>The denser solids move towards the bowl periphery. From there, their ejection happens through the centrifuge cyclone.</p>

  <p>A hydraulic mechanism located under the bowl separation space causes the sludge ejection. This mechanism forces the sliding piston (5) downward, opening the solids ejection ports (6) at the bowl periphery.</p>

  <p>The cyclone reduces the high ejection velocity of the solids.</p>

  <p>Dolphin Centrifuge has Alfa Laval BTPX-205 centrifuge systems in stock for sale.</p>

  <p>Dolphin Centrifuge is the independent specialist in <a href="/alfa-laval-centrifuges/">Alfa Laval</a> centrifuges: remanufactured machines, turnkey systems, parts, and service, built on Alfa Laval experience since 1986 and led by its founder, Sanjay Prabhu, M.S.M.E. Apart from Alfa Laval itself, Dolphin is the reliable source for quality Alfa Laval machines such as the BTPX-205, each one stripped, rebuilt, balanced, and test-run before shipment. Dolphin is an independent remanufacturer and is not affiliated with Alfa Laval.</p>


</ApplicationLayout>
